        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "width": 24,
        "height": 3,
        "properties": {
          "markdown": "## EPICENTRE live app · us-east-1\nBuilt-in AWS metrics only: counts, latencies and token totals, never content. Amazon Bedrock runs the navigator and the explanation; Bedrock Guardrails checks the question (input) and scores the explanation (output); one EC2 instance behind CloudFront serves the app. The Bedrock series are the model ids in config.py and count every caller of those ids in this account (the live app, the evaluation and development runs). **Bedrock model invocation logging is off**, so AWS stores no question or answer; the only thing ever stored is a decision record the investor explicitly seals (private, versioned S3 vault)."
        }
